<p>To mark the 30th anniversary of <em>Infinite Jest</em>, David Foster Wallace&#8217;s sprawling 1996 novel, Brooklyn-based data visualization artist and design professor Christian Swinehart is creating a graphical companion to the book.</p>
<p><a href="https://samizdat.co/digest/">Infinite Digest</a> is a series of interactive visualizations of the novel’s plotlines, characters, and self-referential structure. The first two installments, exploring the book’s <a href="https://samizdat.co/digest/plotlines/">timeline</a> and its many <a href="https://samizdat.co/digest/notes/">footnotes</a>, are currently live, and more will appear over the next few months.</p>
